A brief overview of key terms:

`sap-section`
	It is a section according to the rules:
		1) If there are no sections before and after, then the content itself is a sap-section.
		2) If there are no sections before the content, but there are sections after it,
		then the sap-section is the content after which there is a separator "-" on a separate line.
		3) If there are sections before the content, but no section after it,
		then the sap-section is the content that precedes a separator "-" on a separate line.
		4) If there are sections before and after the content, 
		then the sap-section is the content before and after which the saperator “-” is placed.

`->`
	Then.

(1) A BIT ABOUT RECORDING VERSIONS.
=======================================================================================================

( CATPKG 1.X ) 
	The major version CATPKG 1 is a record of the type of sap-sections that are divided — for example: 
`
CATPKG 1.X
Title
-
Desscription
-
99999
-
Multiple
lines
line 1
line 2
-
-
#option1 option text 1
#option1 option text 2
#option2 option text 3
#option3 option text 4
-
#option1 
#option2 
`

	In the CATPKG 1.X specification, each sap-section has its own designation, for example: 
1 - title; 2 - description; 3 - size; 4 - multiply_line; 5 - empty_section; 6 - options1; 7 - options2.

	The options were added as a standard for MANDATORY declaration of values.

	The patch version (CATPKG 1.0, 1.1, 1.2...) is a template that defines 
how each section is designated; the standards will be described below.

(CATPKG 2.0)
	Version 2.0 is the standard for a more convenient user experience and will be released as part of the release.

(2) CATPKG 1 - OPTIONS DECLORATION
=======================================================================================================

Options are a convenient way to add any additional values to CATPKG 1 formally:
the option starts with "#" and is followed by the option name "#option_name", followed by a space, 
these options are usually written as separate arguments,
and sometimes they can be perceived as a whole piece of data, 
so it's better to take it as "#option_name text for option",
but there is an unspoken standard for transmission in the form of arguments:
"#option_name arg1 arg2 arg3"

(2) CATPKG 1 - SAP-SECTION DECLARATION
=======================================================================================================

The sap-section is a section divided using “-”; 
this section may have different meanings and declarations, so to begin with, 
you can familiarize yourself with the standard declarations:

(Non‑existent section)
`
-
-
`
This is a non‑existent section, and it will return a NULL value,
but it will still be considered a section, so this is a standard way to skip a section if, 
for any reason, the section should be filled in automatically after this. 
A non‑existent section is considered non‑existent
if there is not a single symbol in the 
sap-section (For clarification, check “A brief overview of key terms”).

(Existing section)
`
-

-
`
A section is considered to exist if the SAP section contains at least one character, including a line break.

(Single‑line section)
`
-
Hello world
-
`
A standard single-line section is considered single-line if it contains exactly one line break character “\n” in the sap-section (For clarification, check “A brief overview of key terms”).

(Multiply‑line section)
`
-
Hello world 1
Hello world 2
Hello world 3
-
`
The standard multiply‑line section is a multiply‑line section if the sap-section (For clarification, check “A brief overview of key terms”) contains MORE than one line break character “\n”.

(3) CATPKG 1.0 - PATCH 0, PACKET METADATA
=======================================================================================================
sap-sections designations:
	1 - name
	2 - version
	3 - architecture
	4 - description
	5 - SHA
	6 - size
	7 - dependency
	8 - operations
SAP sections of the declaration:
	1 - (Single‑line section), (Existing section)
	2 - (Single‑line section), (Existing section)
	3 - (Single‑line section) OR (Non‑existent section)
	4 - (Multiply‑line section) OR(Single‑line section) OR (Non‑existent section)
	5 - (Non‑existent section) OR (Single‑line section) -> AFTER ASSEMBLY (Single‑line section)
	6 - (Non‑existent section) OR (Single‑line section) -> AFTER ASSEMBLY (Single‑line section)
	7 - (Multiply‑line section) OR (Non‑existent section)
	8 - (Multiply‑line section) OR (Single‑line section) OR (Non‑existent section)

	SHA and size should be left as (Non‑existent section), architecture can be written as per choice, 
all (Non‑existent section) will be filled in automatically after the package is built.

Information about the sections:
	name 			- Package name;
	version 		- Package version;
	architecture 	- Processor architecture ( Format: aarch64 OR x86_64 );
	description 	- Package description;
	SHA				- The package signature, the minimum integrity indicator of the package, is required for stable operation.
	size			- The size of the package before packaging.
	dependency		- The names of the dependency packages are separated by line breaks.
	operations		- Operations that obscure data describing actions or data for unpacking.

(3.1) CATPKG 1.0 - DECLARATION OF OPERATIONS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(SUBLINK)
`#sublink link -> target`
link - /path/to/link
target - /path/to/target/of/link

(FOLDER)
`#folder folder-path`
Create a dependent folder if it doesn’t exist.

folder-path - path to folder

(3.2) CATPKG 1.0 - DECLARATION OF DEPENDENCY
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
`
catpackage_name1
catpackage_name2
catpackage_name3
`
Package dependencies written with a line break are taken from the PACKAGENAME of the requested package.

(3.3) CATPKG 1.0 - DECLARATION OF VERSION
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
`X.Y.Z`
OR
`X.Y.X-release`

(4) CATPKG 1.1 - PATCH 1, FILE METADATA
=======================================================================================================
sap-sections designations:
	1 - path
SAP sections of the declaration:
	1 - (Single‑line section), (Existing section)

(5) General rules
=======================================================================================================
To indicate the CATPKG version, specify the version in the first line of the file, for example, “CATPKG 1.0”, “CATPKG 1.1”, “CATPKG 2.0”.

